# f1 = count. In the typed copy of the loop `half` is a number that was asked for in front and is still boxed. An equality in the form of numbers takes a boxed number as it is and tells
# int32 from double where it compares: in every turn. Beside a boxed number from in front of the loop it compares raw doubles: the number is unboxed by an operation of its own, which is
# found in front of the loop (here the one that the product made) or built there.
# RUN: walk f1 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: [[boxed]]: number @JSValue = Narrowed
# CHECK: [[raw]]: number @Double = Unbox [[boxed]]
# CHECK: = StrictEq {{*}}, [[raw]] form=Numbers
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
# ANSWER: 7
# ANSWER-NEXT: exited with 0
